An example entry:

bear trap (DL 1)
  effect on player
    If you are polymorphed into an amorphous, non-solid, or small monster,
    no effect.
      "<A/Your> bear trap closes harmlessly through you." (unsolid)
      "<A/Your> bear trap closes harmlessly over you." (small)
    Otherwise, you are trapped and your dexterity is abused. Moving
    diagonally out of the trap will free you in 4 to 7 moves; orthogonal
    moves have only a 1/5 chance of reducing this number.
      "<A/Your> bear trap closes on your <foot>!"
      "You howl in anger!" (polyselfed into owlbear or bugbear)
  effect on monster
    Non-amorphous, solid, larger-than-small monsters are trapped. May anger
    monster if trap set by you.
      "<Monster> is caught in <a/your> bear trap!"
      "You hear the roaring of an angry bear!" (owlbear or bugbear out of
        sight)
    Monsters have a 1/40 chance of releasing themselves each move;
    otherwise, a metallivorous monster may eat the trap to escape.
      "<Monster> eats a bear trap!" (metallivorous, in sight)
  untrapping
    Can be #untrapped, producing a beartrap object that can be applied to
    be set elsewhere. If you are polyselfed into a metallivorous monster,
    you can eat a bear trap you are trapped in. Attempting to web over the
    trap will instead trigger it.

